# RunicAI Evaluation Harness

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"},
  {:runic_ai, path: "~/wrk/runic_ai"}
])

Code.require_file("support/runic_ai_livebook.exs", __DIR__)
```

## What This Notebook Teaches

Evaluation is just another workflow boundary. RunicAI models cases,
expectations, result scoring, metric aggregation, and final run snapshots as
contracts so you can regression-test recipes without hand-inspecting every
turn.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  cases[Evaluation cases] --> harness[Evaluation harness]
  harness --> recipe[Recipe run]
  recipe --> results[Case results]
  results --> aggregate[Aggregate metrics]
  aggregate --> snapshot[Evaluation.Run]
```

## Provider Setup

```elixir
setup = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.inputs()
```

```elixir
model = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_model!(setup)
llm_opts = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.llm_opts(model, max_output_tokens: RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_max_output_tokens(setup))
```

## Define Cases

Expectations are intentionally simple here. Use exact checks for stable
contracts and custom checks for fuzzy behavior.

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Evaluation.Case

cases = [
  Case.new!(
    id: "hello",
    input: %{user: "Say hello in one short sentence."},
    expected: [{:contains_text, "Hello"}]
  ),
  Case.new!(
    id: "runicai",
    input: %{user: "This notebook is about RunicAI. Name the library this notebook is about."},
    expected: [{:contains_text, "RunicAI"}]
  )
]

Kino.DataTable.new(Enum.map(cases, &Map.take(&1, [:id, :input, :expected])))
```

## Run The Harness

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.require_openai_key!()

alias RunicAI.Recipes.{ChatAgentKernel, EvaluationHarness}

eval_run =
  EvaluationHarness.run(cases,
    recipe: ChatAgentKernel,
    recipe_opts: [
      model: model,
      system: "You are a concise assistant. Include requested keywords literally.",
      llm_opts: llm_opts
    ]
  )

eval_run.aggregate
```

```elixir
rows =
  Enum.map(eval_run.results, fn result ->
    scores = result.scores

    %{
      case: result.case_id,
      status: result.status,
      score: Map.get(scores, :overall),
      expectations: "#{Map.get(scores, :passed, 0)}/#{Map.get(scores, :total, 0)}",
      reply: RunicAI.Evaluation.Result.reply_text(result),
      failures: inspect(result.failures)
    }
  end)

Kino.DataTable.new(rows)
```

## Inspect The Evaluation Workflow

```elixir
evaluation_workflow =
  EvaluationHarness.run_workflow(cases,
    recipe: ChatAgentKernel,
    recipe_opts: [
      model: model,
      system: "You are a concise assistant. Include requested keywords literally.",
      llm_opts: llm_opts
    ]
  )

RunicAI.Livebook.WorkflowViz.tabs(evaluation_workflow)
```

## Where To Go Next

Use this harness when changing prompts, tools, guard policies, context windows,
or recipe composition. The same cases can run against deterministic test clients
in CI and live providers during manual release qualification.
